  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF FEMTECH (SRHR) 2025-2027 - UNICEF FEMTECH (SRHR)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNICEF FEMTECH (SRHR) 2025-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till kvinnliga entrepen&#xf6;rer inom tech industrin f&#xf6;r h&#xe4;lsa med fokus p&#xe5; SRHR</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to women entrepreneurs within the female health technology industry with a focus on SRHR</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF and Sida has signed a multiyear agreement (2025-2027) for a new initiative run by UNICEF&apos;s Innovation Hub in Stockholm. The aim is to provide support to the female health tech industry in Africa, commonly known as FemTech. The initiative will be run by UNICEF&apos;s Innovation Hub in Stockholm and the Venture Fund.

The female health technology industry, focuses on leveraging technology to
address women&apos;s health and wellbeing needs. In recent years, the FemTech
industry has seen impressive growth encompassing technologies aimed at
enhancing women and girls sexual and reproductive health and rights (SRHR)
with products, services, and solutions predominantly built for, by, and with
women and girls. While there has been a notable growth in Femtech founders
and solutions across the industry, limited attention has been paid to founder
talent in emerging markets and designing solutions that solve the diverse health
needs of women and girls in low and middle income countries.


The objective of this initiative is to:
-Increase awareness and access to, and respect for, sexual and reproductive
health and rights (SRHR) for all, to empower girls and young women
-Improve the availability and quality of healthcare products and services for
girls and women 
-Increase investment flows to these solutions</narrative>
  </description>
